{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release","id":1476179,"title":"Operative's Dossier pre-release","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-10T17:52:34-08:00","id":1476179,"title":"Operative's Dossier pre-release","content":"It's out! I have just downloaded it, and I expect to be engrossed in it for the next few hours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T18:14:03-08:00","id":1476182,"title":"","content":"I look forward to your 7000th post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-10T21:06:07-08:00","id":1476190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476182#post1476182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I look forward to your 7000th post.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll do my best to make it a good one. <br /> <br /> <u><b>The Operative's Dossier</b></u><br /> Throughout the book, there are Disputed Data boxes designed to facilitate different takes on the content, depending on what metaplot elements you do or don't feature in your chronicle. They're very much into \u201cit's your game; do as you wish\u201d. <br /> <br /> <b>Chapter one: Constructs and Symposiums</b><br /> This chapter has five sections in it: the Arcology X Project (Sejong, Republic of Korea), the Multinational Military Development Site (Northern Territory, Australia), Terranorming Research and Application (Lake Delton, Wisconsin), Ultima Thule, and the Experimental Station Symposium. Despite the being five of them, they are <i>not</i> aligned with individual Conventions. That said, they do have leanings: Arcology X is very much the story of things the Progenitors would like; MMDS has a very Iteration X vibe; Terranorming Research and Assocation is very much an NWO thing; Ultima Thule lands into Void Engineers interests; and and the Experimental Station Symposium is a Syndicate operation. <br /> <br /> <b>Chapter two: Unlikely Allies</b><br /> Five sections there, too: the Council of Nine Mystick Traditions, Dissident Permutations, the Disparate Alliance, Orphans and the Unaligned, and Anomalous Allies. <br /> <br /> \u2022 The first section is a deep dive into the Ascension Truce metaplot option from Technocracy Reloaded. <br /> \u2022 Dissident Permutations deals with factions within the Union who are at odds with the Union as a whole: several Cross-Convention Initiatives (the Challenge Fate Foundation, the Department of Metahuman Studies, the Existential Threats Directorate, and Panopticon), the Friends of Courage, Project Invictus, and the Special Information Security Division (a spiritual successor to the Special Projects Division). The Disputed Data for the SISD includes an option near and dear to my heart: rather than being part of the corruption of Pentex, it suggests that the SISD might \u201cmerely\u201d be monitoring, collecting, and studying deviant technology, such as those created by the likes of Etherites and VAs. <br /> \u2022 The Disparate Alliance section begins with the Black Daggers (what, you thought that the Ksirafai <i>abandoned</i> the Union?). It then goes into further detail about the Challenge Fate Foundation, and how the Disparates (and others) may have trouble believing that there's an honest-to-goodness good guys faction within the Union. The Cassandra Complex, meanwhile, is aiding the Disparate Alliance in its efforts to purge the Union of its corruption. The Friends of Courage also get revisited, in terms of how they're looking at the Alliance as a possible new option for Ascension. Both of the Enlightened Science factions being courted by the Alliance (Navalon and Mokteshaf Al Nour) are addressed. Finally, Project Invictus is <i>also</i> looking for allies among the Disparates. <br /> \u2022 Orphans and the Unaligned: these terms are synonyms, though \u201cOrphans\u201d carries pejorative connotations that \u201cUnaligned\u201d doesn't. As well, the point is made that as much as the Union likes to think that it has a monopoly on Enlightened Science, it doesn't: not only are there Etherites and VAs who aren't so far gone into \u201cdeviant technology\u201d that they still might qualify as Scientists, but there are Unaligned Enlightened Scientists as well. The section goes through various stages of life for an Unaligned Scientist and how he or she might slip through the cracks and manage <i>not</i> to be recruited by the Union. <br /> \u2022 Finally, the section on Anomalous Allies provides three sample characters \u2014 a vampire, a werewolf, and a ghost(?). <br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 3: Digital Web 3.0</b><br /> The big new thing that DW3.0 brings to the fore is Augmented Reality. This is followed by a rundown on how the Digital Web works, Social Media and the Agent, and the Dark (Digital) Web. <br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 4: Technomancer's Toybox</b><br /> <i>Adjustments</i>: deviance potential evaluation, distribution management, ecological harmonization, generate emotional field array, predictive analysis, remote access, save file index, Schrodinger's parcel, system havoc, white out.<br /> <i>Alternate Perceptions</i>: Augmented Reality, Near Infrared, Pulse Mapping, Thermal. <br /> <i>Procedures</i>: Anti-Hemophagic Saline, Atomic Override, Force Compliance, Multipartite Host Infection, Pen Lance, Thanatos. <br /> <i>Gadjets</i>: 30 second start, adaptive combat analytics interface, brown paper bag, conversation emulator, field medical kit, nanite tags, Urban navigation tool, augmented reality smart glasses, pocket drone modifications, portable perimeter fence, DOUG upgrade, reverse temporal projector, automated construction, isolated strand, turbulent displacement field, wormhole generator, and tropic perception field alteration, node denial device.<br /> <i>MMDS Prototype Technology</i>: paradox sink, surveillance nanites, Quantum State ion weapon mark 1.<br /> <br /> Also in this section is a subsection about creating constructs and chantries. And a section on Terranorming. <br /> <br /> <b>Chapter 5: Mission Statements</b><br /> <i>Mission One: Hope</i><br /> <i>Mission Two: The Miracle of Creation</i><br /> <i>Mission Three: Progress is a Process </i><br /> <i>Mission Four: Cats in the Dox Box</i><br /> <i>Mission Five: This Equipment Has Not Been Tested</i><br /> <i>Mission Six: Wounds of War</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-11-2022, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T17:16:27-08:00","id":1476241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476190#post1476190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Chapter one: Constructs and Symposiums</b><br /> This chapter has five sections in it: the Arcology X Project (Sejong, Republic of Korea), the Multinational Military Development Site (Northern Territory, Australia), Terranorming Research and Application (Lake Delton, Wisconsin), Ultima Thule, and the Experimental Station Symposium. Despite the being five of them, they are <i>not</i> aligned with individual Conventions. That said, they do have leanings: Arcology X is very much the story of things the Progenitors would like; MMDS has a very Iteration X vibe; Terranorming Research and Assocation is very much an NWO thing; Ultima Thule lands into Void Engineers interests; and and the Experimental Station Symposium is a Syndicate operation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coincidentally, I already have an Arcology with strong Progenitor influence in my campaign. It will definitely be nice to have some constructs that I can just grab, read, adapt and the tell my players, &quot;infiltrate this&quot; (since they're Traditions).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476190#post1476190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Chapter two: Unlikely Allies</b><br /> Five sections there, too: the Council of Nine Mystick Traditions, Dissident Permutations, the Disparate Alliance, Orphans and the Unaligned, and Anomalous Allies.<br /> <br /> \u2022 The first section is a deep dive into the Ascension Truce metaplot option from Technocracy Reloaded.<br /> \u2022 Dissident Permutations deals with factions within the Union who are at odds with the Union as a whole: several Cross-Convention Initiatives (the Challenge Fate Foundation, the Department of Metahuman Studies, the Existential Threats Directorate, and Panopticon), the Friends of Courage, Project Invictus, and the Special Information Security Division (a spiritual successor to the Special Projects Division). The Disputed Data for the SISD includes an option near and dear to my heart: rather than being part of the corruption of Pentex, it suggests that the SISD might \u201cmerely\u201d be monitoring, collecting, and studying deviant technology, such as those created by the likes of Etherites and VAs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've also ditched Pentex in a campaign with mountaintop removal mining as a story element and since I'm playing an Etherite, his estranged mentor will be SISD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476190#post1476190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 The Disparate Alliance section begins with the Black Daggers (what, you thought that the Ksirafai <i>abandoned</i> the Union?). It then goes into further detail about the Challenge Fate Foundation, and how the Disparates (and others) may have trouble believing that there's an honest-to-goodness good guys faction within the Union. The Cassandra Complex, meanwhile, is aiding the Disparate Alliance in its efforts to purge the Union of its corruption. The Friends of Courage also get revisited, in terms of how they're looking at the Alliance as a possible new option for Ascension. Both of the Enlightened Science factions being courted by the Alliance (Navalon and Mokteshaf Al Nour) are addressed. Finally, Project Invictus is <i>also</i> looking for allies among the Disparates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they provide associative relationship maps to help understand the chapter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476190#post1476190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Orphans and the Unaligned: these terms are synonyms, though \u201cOrphans\u201d carries pejorative connotations that \u201cUnaligned\u201d doesn't. As well, the point is made that as much as the Union likes to think that it has a monopoly on Enlightened Science, it doesn't: not only are there Etherites and VAs who aren't so far gone into \u201cdeviant technology\u201d that they still might qualify as Scientists, but there are Unaligned Enlightened Scientists as well. The section goes through various stages of life for an Unaligned Scientist and how he or she might slip through the cracks and manage <i>not</i> to be recruited by the Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Unaligned scientist isn't held back by Control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476190#post1476190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Finally, the section on Anomalous Allies provides three sample characters \u2014 a vampire, a werewolf, and a ghost(?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts are always fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476190#post1476190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Chapter 3: Digital Web 3.0</b><br /> The big new thing that DW3.0 brings to the fore is Augmented Reality. This is followed by a rundown on how the Digital Web works, Social Media and the Agent, and the Dark (Digital) Web.</div> </div> </div> </div>Social Media and the Agent - Does it get into dating apps like Tinder?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476190#post1476190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also in this section is a subsection about creating constructs and chantries. And a section on Terranorming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the book is supposed to be a players' guide, I'm guessing that it is how players themselves would go about creating a Construct. Is that the case?<br /> <br /> Terranorming is no small thing, both as an undertaking and a concept. Are you happy with the level of detail in the section?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 03-11-2022, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T18:29:56-08:00","id":1476246,"title":"","content":"I have submitted some errata concerning the Terranorming section. As written, it's a six-step process: <br /> 1. Declaration: side what change you want to make (the Thoughtspace) and where you want to make it.<br /> 2. Recon: identify any deviations from the desired Thoughtspace. Essentially, this involves identifying reality Deviants who would actively opposed the change.<br /> 3. Repriming: dedicate a Node or a Venture to the Terranorming. The racing should reflect the size of the era that you are attempting to Terranorm. <br /> 4. Clearing: remove the obstacles identified in step two.<br /> 5. Holding: maintain the desired status quo for a length of time determined by the aforementioned node rating, from one month for a 1 Dot node to 50 years for a Five Dot node.<br /> 6. Capping: seal the change, so that it no longer needs the node or venture to persist.<br /> <br /> There's also a box to the effect that this process was formalized by the technocracy, but is informally followed by everyone who engages in what the technocracy would call Terranorming. <br /> <br /> The errata that I suggested involves a couple of things: <br /> <br /> first, add a step to actually implement the change. This should include a page reference to M20 pp.616\u2013617, which discusses the process of Paradigm shifting a reality zone. As written, the sequence doesn't include anything proactive; just making plans and clearing obstacles.<br /> <br /> Second, make the repriming step optional. I can see it being harder to Terranorm without a node or Venture backing you up; which I would represent in game terms by having the holding time take longer (my suggestion is to calculate the time as one dot higher if you don't actually have any repriming); but it shouldn't be impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T16:04:52-08:00","id":1476293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476246#post1476246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI have submitted some errata concerning the Terranorming section. As written, it's a six-step process:<br /> 1. Declaration: side what change you want to make (the Thoughtspace) and where you want to make it.<br /> 2. Recon: identify any deviations from the desired Thoughtspace. Essentially, this involves identifying reality Deviants who would actively opposed the change.<br /> 3. Repriming: dedicate a Node or a Venture to the Terranorming. The racing should reflect the size of the era that you are attempting to Terranorm.<br /> 4. Clearing: remove the obstacles identified in step two.<br /> 5. Holding: maintain the desired status quo for a length of time determined by the aforementioned node rating, from one month for a 1 Dot node to 50 years for a Five Dot node.<br /> 6. Capping: seal the change, so that it no longer needs the node or venture to persist.<br /> <br /> There's also a box to the effect that this process was formalized by the technocracy, but is informally followed by everyone who engages in what the technocracy would call Terranorming.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm trying to understand the relationship between three variables (Area Size, Node Rating and Length of Time) and even what Length of Time refers to. Area Size determines the required Node Rating. It does not seem clear how to interpret Length of Time, which is based on Node Rating (so, ultimately, Area Size). <br /> &quot;5. Holding: maintain the desired status quo for a length of time determined by the aforementioned node rating, from one month for a 1 Dot node to 50 years for a Five Dot node.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you want to to Terranorm the largest geographic area, you must use a powerful Node AND hold the area for 50 years? If you want to Terranorm your immediate neighborhood (lets say), you only need a Node of 1 AND to hold the area for 1 month?<br /> <br /> That would mean a Mage using a pizza parlor as a Venture could Terranorm a small area around it in only one month, with that having a degree of permanence. This, even if that Mage were cleared from the area, would interfere with the efforts of a group of Mages trying to flip the region using a more powerful Node or Venture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476246#post1476246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The errata that I suggested involves a couple of things:<br /> <br /> first, add a step to actually implement the change. This should include a page reference to M20 pp.616\u2013617, which discusses the process of Paradigm shifting a reality zone. As written, the sequence doesn't include anything proactive; just making plans and clearing obstacles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. I would even say that the Ascension Truce, which I use, could not be a serious metaplot element if it were impossible to Terranorm the largest area without clearing a whole region for fifty years, &quot;Gun&quot; being the 10th Sphere. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476246#post1476246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, make the repriming step optional. I can see it being harder to Terranorm without a node or Venture backing you up; which I would represent in game terms by having the holding time take longer (my suggestion is to calculate the time as one dot higher if you don't actually have any repriming); but it shouldn't be impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say scaling down the intensity of the change, putting emphasis on subtlety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T16:21:47-08:00","id":1476296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476293#post1476293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to understand the relationship between three variables (Area Size, Node Rating and Length of Time) and even what Length of Time refers to. Area Size determines the required Node Rating. It does not seem clear how to interpret Length of Time, which is based on Node Rating (so, ultimately, Area Size). <br /> &amp;quot;5. Holding: maintain the desired status quo for a length of time determined by the aforementioned node rating, from one month for a 1 Dot node to 50 years for a Five Dot node.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> If you want to to Terranorm the largest geographic area, you must use a powerful Node AND hold the area for 50 years? If you want to Terranorm your immediate neighborhood (lets say), you only need a Node of 1 AND to hold the area for 1 month?<br /> <br /> That would mean a Mage using a pizza parlor as a Venture could Terranorm a small area around it in only one month, with that having a degree of permanence. This, even if that Mage were cleared from the area, would interfere with the efforts of a group of Mages trying to flip the region using a more powerful Node or Venture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. There's a comment near the end to the effect that the 20th century demonstrated the folly of trying to Terranorm too much, as too many things can go wrong. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476293#post1476293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely. I would even say that the Ascension Truce, which I use, could not be a serious metaplot element if it were impossible to Terranorm the largest area without clearing a whole region for fifty years, &amp;quot;Gun&amp;quot; being the 10th Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is that it's easier to do it region by region, with a balance between not going too small (because you'd have to repeat the process a lot of times) and not going too large (because it's too easy to disrupt). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476293#post1476293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say scaling down the intensity of the change, putting emphasis on subtlety.</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory, sure; in practice, how would you quantify that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T18:25:19-08:00","id":1476302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476296#post1476296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In theory, sure; in practice, how would you quantify that?</div> </div> </div> </div>With some difficulty, but we are already talking about changing how reality functions and then variances from place to place. Do they reference Earthly Foundations in the bit about Thoughtspace? <br /> <br /> If meeting the criteria for Node allows the greatest Thoughtspace, then that should be a specified number of changes. I would say between three and five changes that must not deviate too dramatically from Earthly Foundations. You could subtract from the number of changes to reduce or eliminate the need for a Node. <br /> <br /> If it is just binary, as in &quot;Node Required&quot; or &quot;No Node Required&quot;, then you could have two categories of change: Social and Physical. The Mage(s) without a Node would have to chose between one of those two. An actual example that players are likely to consider would be introducing robots into a community. The first category is the changes in Physical Laws that allow those robots to function well. The Second would be changes in Social Laws that facilitate their acceptance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T19:51:07-08:00","id":1476306,"title":"","content":"Will there be the option of getting a print copy? I personally prefer physical books, and it would be nice to be able to buy a printed copy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T13:07:40-07:00","id":1476336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476306#post1476306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will there be the option of getting a print copy? I personally prefer physical books, and it would be nice to be able to buy a printed copy.</div> </div> </div> </div>As always, the answer is yes there will be PoD when it\u2019s released on Drivethru.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T16:45:21-07:00","id":1476348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1476179-operative-s-dossier-pre-release?p=1476336#post1476336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As always, the answer is yes there will be PoD when it\u2019s released on Drivethru.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that news.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T01:36:09-07:00","id":1476367,"title":"","content":"I must say, I really like the section about Cooperation with the traditions, disparates, and independents. It won't be easy, but it shows a Technocracy aware of their hubris and (in theory) willing to change their ways. Nevertheless, I also like how each faction within the Union has their let's say &quot;unique&quot; viewpoint about how this cooperation would, and wouldn't, work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}